From bbd845a49c0e358206b54c2c1114958e55ace370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 09:35:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=202a=20Wave=20B:=20Twilio=20SMS=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20auto-reply=20+=2024hr=20review=20request?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Migration 007: sms_events (delivery log, Twilio SID, template,
  lead/customer/job FKs) + scheduled_sms (pending queue drained by
  cron). RLS: authenticated-only SELECT, service-role INSERT/UPDATE.
- src/lib/twilio.ts: lazy Twilio client, sendSms() logs every attempt
  to sms_events (success or failure). Throws on Twilio error after
  recording the event so callers decide whether to fire-and-forget.
- src/lib/sms-templates.ts: leadAutoReply + reviewRequest. Every body
  ends with "Reply STOP to opt out." to stay TCPA-compliant. Review
  URL from NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REVIEW_URL env (optional).
- /api/leads POST fires SMS auto-reply after the Supabase insert +
  Resend emails. Fire-and-forget, won't block the response.
- /api/jobs/[id] PATCH inserts a scheduled_sms row with send_at = +24h
  when a job transitions to 'completed'. Silently skips customers
  without a phone.
- New cron route /api/cron/send-scheduled-sms drains up to 50 pending
  rows per run, marks sent/failed, links sms_event_id. Dual-auth
  (Bearer CRON_SECRET or Supabase cookie) matches scrape-permits.
- vercel.json: hourly cron schedule.
- Dashboard fetches latest sms_events per lead; LeadsTable renders a
  second pill (📱 Sent / Delivered / Failed) below the email pill,
  gated on `mounted` to avoid hydration drift.

Env vars required post-merge: TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN,
TWILIO_FROM, NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REVIEW_URL (optional).
